   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Artfat H3 Face Refine (chunked) - example\nSharpens small / far faces in a finished **MiniMax H3** video and keeps lip-sync, expression and skin tone.\n\n**Connect**\n- **video**: Load Video (pick or upload your finished mp4). Its audio is kept and guides the mouth. *(video_path is only a fallback when this is not connected.)*\n- **model**: the H3 model you generated the video with, with *MiniMaxH3SigmaShift 12/3*.\n- **vae / audio_vae**: H3 video and audio VAE.\n- **face_ref** (optional): a picture of the person's face. Empty = the face from the first frame.\n\n**Prompt = only the face.** The model sees only the face crop, so write the expression from your shot prompt: eyes, brows, mouth, the spoken line, laughter. Nothing about body, clothes or scene. Example:\n> <Subject 1> (S1) looks into the camera, raises her eyebrows in disbelief and physically speaks: <d>[English] ...your line...</d> Right after the line she bursts out laughing, her eyes squint, then smiles.\n\nA generic prompt still works, but it smooths expressions the shot asked for (raised / knitted brows).\n\n**Defaults that tested best**\n- denoise 0.5 (lower keeps the expression closer, higher redraws more)\n- sampler uni_pc, beta, 8 steps\n- SAM3 threshold 0.15 (higher loses the face on some frames -> jiggle)\n- VOSR2 polish on, tone match on\n- chunk 145 frames: long videos run in chunks, memory does not grow with length\n\n**Needs**: ComfyUI-H3-FaceRefine (Carasibana), MaskVidExperiments, ComfyUI_LC_MaskMaker_nodes (VOSR2), ComfyUI-GGUF, SAM 3.1 checkpoint.\n\nFree & open source (GPL-3). Output: output/FaceRefine/."
   ]
  }
